 "notes": [
  "Parts are unchanged from step 1.",
  "The onboard LED on pin 13 is part of the Uno, so there is no external LED or resistor. Pin 2 uses the internal pull-up (INPUT_PULLUP).",
  "The image shows the pushbutton straddling the centre gap with its legs in columns 10 and 12. I used the catalogue's naming, where bank 't' is rows a-e and bank 'b' is rows f-j. The button therefore sits in rows f (bank b) and e (bank t).",
  "The image does not show which button legs are joined internally. I took the two legs in column 10 as side 1 and the two in column 12 as side 2. Pressing the button then joins the pin 2 column to the GND column, as the schematic shows.",
  "The teal wire goes from Uno pin 2 to column 10, row c (10t.c). The black wire goes from the Uno power-header GND (the second GND, GND.2) to column 12, row c (12t.c)."
